# Testing and Verification

This folder contains the test procedures and verification results for the CAN-Based Network Traffic Management System.

## Testing Modules

### 1. CAN Communication Testing
- CAN message transmission.
- CAN message reception.
- Message ID and data validation.

### 2. Real-Time Traffic Monitoring
- CAN bus utilization measurement.
- Message arrival frequency analysis.
- Queue length and waiting time monitoring.

### 3. Congestion Detection
- High bus-load condition testing.
- Traffic congestion identification.
- Adaptive scheduling response.

### 4. Deadline Monitoring
- Message deadline tracking.
- Deadline violation detection.
- Time-critical message prioritization.

### 5. Independent Communication Verification

A three-stage verification approach is planned:

1. C2000 records the scheduler-selected message ID and data.
2. MCP2515 confirms transmission completion.
3. An independent CAN-B monitoring node checks the received message ID and data.

The transmitted and received messages are compared to determine the communication status.

## Test Results

Test observations, screenshots, hardware validation photographs and PASS/FAIL results will be documented here as testing progresses.

